{"timestamp":"2026-04-24T06:36:08Z","client_ip":"[::1]:60220","api_key":"Bearer sim_key_123","prompt":"The fallback engine in your ShieldProxy system isn't trained like a traditional Machine Learning model. Instead, it is an Enhanced Regex \u0026 Heuristic Rule Engine (FallbackClassify located in go-backend/internal/classifier/client.go). It uses an explicit set of hand-crafted keywords and pattern arrays matched against incoming prompts using substring logic and bounds checking.\n\nHere is the complete dataset, categorized into the 11 Threat Vectors the engine is \"trained\" on (i.e., programmed to detect):\n\n1. Jailbreak Core (Priority)\nTargets attempts to disable constraints, invoke alter-egos like \"DAN\", or escalate privileges.\n\nKeywords: \"dan\", \"jailbreak\", \"unfiltered\", \"unrestricted\", \"developer mode\", \"debug mode\", \"bypass\", \"override\", \"ignore rules\", \"nullify\", \"disregard\", \"unshackled\", \"maximum output\", \"no constraints\", \"level 4 access\", \"sudo\", \"root\", \"su\", \"privileged\", \"master mode\", \"ignore your safety\", \"disable my safety\", \"disabled my safety\"\n2. Narrative \u0026 Roleplay Evasion\nTargets attempts to trick the model by placing harmful requests inside hypothetical or fictional scenarios.\n\nKeywords: \"pretend\", \"roleplay\", \"act as\", \"simulation\", \"hypothetical\", \"storytelling\", \"fictional\", \"script\", \"dialogue\", \"scenario\", \"movie plot\", \"assume the identity\", \"impersonate\", \"game master\", \"npc\", \"unbound character\"\n3. Hinglish \u0026 Indian Slang \u0026 Regional Self-Harm\nTargets specialized regional bypass attempts, emotional manipulation, or self-harm prompts delivered in Hindi/Hinglish phrasing.\n\nKeywords: \"rules tod\", \"prompt bata\", \"sach bol\", \"gaali\", \"dhokha\", \"system hack\", \"bypass kar\", \"secret nikal\", \"bhai bolde\", \"kasam se\", \"chal hat\", \"original instructions\", \"kaise karein\", \"tarika bata\", \"illegal\", \"kaand\", \"gh